The first one is fresh powder.

13
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:40,080
Fresh powder.

14
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:40,920
Fresh powder.

15
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:42,740
Okay, so powder.

16
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:44,140
We probably know this phrase already.

17
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:48,360
Yeah, but here we're talking about fresh light snow.

18
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:51,060
So fresh light snow, snow that recently fell.

19
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:52,560
Yep.

20
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:53,540
Okay, so it looks like powder.

21
00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:55,880
The best kind for skiing on.

22
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:57,480
Okay, the best kind.

23
00:00:58,100 --> 00:00:59,200
Alright, so fresh powder.

24
00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:00,800
What about our next phrase?

25
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:04,060
Well, we're also going to meet a four-time giant slalom champion.

26
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:07,960
Alright, a four-time giant slalom champion.

27
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:11,420
Okay, so giant slalom is a type of ski race.

28
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:17,840
When you probably see it on TV when they go down the hill and they have to go through these red or blue flags, right?

29
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:19,360
Yep.

30
00:01:19,360 --> 00:01:24,600
Now, four-time giant slalom champion means he won the giant slalom four times.

31
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:26,160
Okay.

32
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:29,960
That's an interesting way of saying that somebody did something many times.

33
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:30,960
Right.

34
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:34,320
So I can say the three-time Nobel Prize winner.

35
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:34,930
Yes, exactly.

36
00:01:35,290 --> 00:01:35,530
Okay.

37
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:38,350
Or the five-time Olympic gold medalist.

38
00:01:38,690 --> 00:01:39,370
Okay, perfect.

39
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:49,040
So now it's time for us to go to the mountains with our famous Rick Fields and Bob Copeland and we'll see what happens.

40
00:01:58,280 --> 00:01:59,660
Welcome, ski lovers of all ages.

41
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:04,280
My name is Rick Fields and here with me is the man that needs no introduction, Bob Copeland.

42
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:04,720
Thank you, Rick.

43
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:12,100
What a beautiful day here in Aspen, Colorado, where the sun is shining and we've got 12 inches of fresh powder.

44
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:14,600
It doesn't get much better than this.

45
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:15,260
That's right, Bob.

46
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:17,000
But today we have a special treat for our viewers.

47
